    "text": "Q: Explain the use of RST flag in TCP header (AKTU 2021-22) RST Flag: > The TCP RST flag indicates that connection should be immediately terminated. > If in case, the connection has already been closed from one side (side A) and the other side (side B) suddenly comes back and wishes to continue the session for data transfer, host (side A) usually responds by sending a RST packet back to the same connection and stating that Dodanger interested in data transfer. RST bit will be set to high in the TCP header flag. (O RY, 1. The packet 1s an initial SYN packet trying to establish a connection to a server port on @) process 1s listening. 2. The packet arrives on a TCP connection that was previously established but the local application has already closed its socket or exited and the OS has closed the socket. 3.Other circumstances such as attempts to hijack a TCP connection.",
